 "text": "Hi! How's your day treating you? You won't look stupid. People there are usually just as excited as you to be out. ask for a fork and knife right away. Lots of people do, and the staff is used to it. Dress casually but decently. There's usually a sign on door that tells you what they want. Ask for recommendations. Chefs love telling stories about their dish, especially with a newcomer. You don't have to. A chef's dish is usually the one with the biggest description, so pick something that sounds interesting.",
